# The age PUBLIC key that fuzz-nightly.yml encrypts every finding to (owner decision (62)(1)).
# The private key is held by the owner and is never in this repository or in CI.
#
# While the line below is the placeholder, tools/fuzz-seal-finding.sh REFUSES to seal or upload
# anything (exit 4, a workflow warning): nothing is published and nothing is kept. The owner's
# key swap is the only change needed:
#
#   age-keygen -o ~/burrow-security/fuzz-crash.key
#
# then replace the PLACEHOLDER line with the `# public key: age1...` value it prints (the bare
# age1... string, nothing else on the line). Decrypt a downloaded artifact with
#   age -d -i ~/burrow-security/fuzz-crash.key <target>.age | tar -x
PLACEHOLDER-NOT-A-KEY-REPLACE-WITH-age-keygen-PUBLIC-KEY
